{"type":"inlineCode","value":"customElements"},{"type":"text","value":" is available."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"presentation-and-rendering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Presentation and rendering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.class"},{"type":"text","value":" and the string "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.style"},{"type":"text","value":" apply to the inner\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".ts-chart-host"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.className"},{"type":"text","value":" applies to the rendered chart surface.\nThe custom element starts with SVG and can compose marks that use\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canvasChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":". Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderSvg"},{"type":"text","value":" to replace SVG serialization without\nreplacing the shared host."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exports: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineChartElement"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartCommonProps"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartPresentationProps"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartProps"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartDefinition"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartPoint"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tooltip-body-composition","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tooltip body composition"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.renderTooltipBody"},{"type":"text","value":" to return any Lit-renderable value. Include its\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultBody"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TemplateResult"},{"type":"text","value":" to retain native rows and swatches. The shared\nhost owns focus, placement, portaling, inert transient state, pinning, and\ndismissal; Lit owns the rendered template lifecycle."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./reference/chart.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/chart-definitions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chart Definition API"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"lifecycle","text":"Lifecycle","level":2},{"id":"browser-and-server-status","text":"Browser and server status","level":2},{"id":"presentation-and-rendering","text":"Presentation and rendering","level":2},{"id":"tooltip-body-composition","text":"Tooltip body composition","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```sh\npnpm add @tanstack/charts lit\n```\n\nRegister the element once:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChartElement } from '@tanstack/charts/lit'\n\ndefineChartElement()\n```\n\nPass chart options as a property:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n\nhtml`<tanstack-chart\n  .options=${{\n    definition: defineChart(createRevenueChart(rows), { tooltip }),\n    ariaLabel: 'Revenue by month',\n  }}\n></tanstack-chart>`\n```\n\nThe element uses light DOM so it inherits application fonts and chart theme\nvariables. Use a custom tag name with `defineChartElement('revenue-chart')`.\n\n## Lifecycle\n\nThe element prerenders through one shared adapter controller, mounts after its\nfirst update, forwards replacement `options` values, and destroys the mounted\nhost when disconnected. Reconnecting the same element mounts the controller\nagain. Assign options as a property; chart configuration is not reflected to\nHTML attributes.\n\n## Browser and server status\n\nThe verified package contract covers browser registration, update,\ndisconnect, and reconnect behavior. Lit SSR and hydration are not yet part of\nthe adapter's tested public contract. Call `defineChartElement` only where\n`customElements` is available.\n\n## Presentation and rendering\n\n`options.class` and the string `options.style` apply to the inner\n`.ts-chart-host`; `options.className` applies to the rendered chart surface.\nThe custom element starts with SVG and can compose marks that use\n`canvasChartRenderer`. Use `renderSvg` to replace SVG serialization without\nreplacing the shared host.\n\nExports: `Chart`, `defineChartElement`, `ChartCommonProps`,\n`ChartPresentationProps`, `ChartProps`, `ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext`,\n`ChartDefinition`, and `ChartPoint`.\n\n## Tooltip body composition\n\nSet `options.renderTooltipBody` to return any Lit-renderable value. Include its\n`defaultBody` `TemplateResult` to retain native rows and swatches. The shared\nhost owns focus, placement, portaling, inert transient state, pinning, and\ndismissal; Lit owns the rendered template lifecycle.\n\nSee the [`Chart` reference](./reference/chart.md) and\n[Chart Definition API](../../reference/chart-definitions.md).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Lit Adapter\ndescription: Render TanStack Charts with a light-DOM Lit custom element.\n---\n\n```sh\npnpm add @tanstack/charts lit\n```\n\nRegister the element once:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChartElement } from '@tanstack/charts/lit'\n\ndefineChartElement()\n```\n\nPass chart options as a property:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n\nhtml`<tanstack-chart\n  .options=${{\n    definition: defineChart(createRevenueChart(rows), { tooltip }),\n    ariaLabel: 'Revenue by month',\n  }}\n></tanstack-chart>`\n```\n\nThe element uses light DOM so it inherits application fonts and chart theme\nvariables. Use a custom tag name with `defineChartElement('revenue-chart')`.\n\n## Lifecycle\n\nThe element prerenders through one shared adapter controller, mounts after its\nfirst update, forwards replacement `options` values, and destroys the mounted\nhost when disconnected. Reconnecting the same element mounts the controller\nagain. Assign options as a property; chart configuration is not reflected to\nHTML attributes.\n\n## Browser and server status\n\nThe verified package contract covers browser registration, update,\ndisconnect, and reconnect behavior. Lit SSR and hydration are not yet part of\nthe adapter's tested public contract. Call `defineChartElement` only where\n`customElements` is available.\n\n## Presentation and rendering\n\n`options.class` and the string `options.style` apply to the inner\n`.ts-chart-host`; `options.className` applies to the rendered chart surface.\nThe custom element starts with SVG and can compose marks that use\n`canvasChartRenderer`. Use `renderSvg` to replace SVG serialization without\nreplacing the shared host.\n\nExports: `Chart`, `defineChartElement`, `ChartCommonProps`,\n`ChartPresentationProps`, `ChartProps`, `ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext`,\n`ChartDefinition`, and `ChartPoint`.\n\n## Tooltip body composition\n\nSet `options.renderTooltipBody` to return any Lit-renderable value. Include its\n`defaultBody` `TemplateResult` to retain native rows and swatches. The shared\nhost owns focus, placement, portaling, inert transient state, pinning, and\ndismissal; Lit owns the rendered template lifecycle.\n\nSee the [`Chart` reference](./reference/chart.md) and\n[Chart Definition API](../../reference/chart-definitions.md).\n"}
